cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite this software record and the scientific
  publications for each method used. See docs/citation-guide.md.
type: software
title: "NEGF-TDPSCBA: Time-Dependent Quantum Transport with Frozen-SCBA Phonons"
authors:
  - family-names: Rossignol
    given-names: Louis
  - family-names: Guo
    given-names: Hong
repository-code: "https://github.com/louis-rsgl/NEGF-TDPSCBA"
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of time-dependent nonequilibrium Green-function
  transport for a scalar electronic level with Lorentzian finite-bandwidth
  leads and one stationary phonon mode. Stationary weak-Born or
  self-consistent-Born electron-phonon kernels are frozen during downward,
  upward, and square voltage pulses; the retarded sector uses a validated
  minimal-pole representation.
keywords:
  - nonequilibrium Green functions
  - time-dependent quantum transport
  - electron-phonon interaction
  - self-consistent Born approximation
  - finite-bandwidth leads
  - minimal pole representation
